thinking
**Identifying run log update challenge**

The run log records every executed command, so running commands after committing will keep modifying it and prevent a clean final repo state. I'll need to commit all run log changes once at the end and avoid further commands to preserve a clean snapshot.
thinking
**Analyzing run log and clean tree conflict**

Confirming a clean tree after commit conflicts with run log auto-updates on each command. The best plan is to run `git status` before the final commit to verify cleanliness, commit all changes including run log, then avoid any further commands—accepting that after commit no tool calls run so the tree remains clean going forward.
thinking
**Confirming clean state limited by run log updates**

